body:
Several pages used one-time `useEffect` fetches that never re-ran after mutations, leaving stale data until a manual reload. All lookup data (services, vehicles, profiles, roles) is now live-queried via Supabase realtime subscriptions.

## Changes

- **`useStaff.ts`** — `useProfilesByRole` was a fire-once fetch. Added `postgres_changes` subscriptions on `profiles` + `user_roles` so the employee/manager list updates the moment a new account is created.

- **`customer/ServiceHistory.tsx`, `customer/MyBookings.tsx`, `customer/Dashboard.tsx`** — Static `Promise.all` fetches for services and vehicles replaced with `useLiveTable`; ID→record maps derived via `useMemo`.

- **`customer/BookService.tsx`** — Services and vehicles now use `useLiveTable`; first-vehicle auto-selection moved to a `useEffect` watching the live data array.

- **`manager/Employees.tsx`** — Removed the manual `refreshKey` state/`key` prop hack that forced a remount after adding staff. Realtime in `useProfilesByRole` makes it redundant.

## Pattern applied

```tsx
// Before: one-time fetch, stale after mutations
useEffect(() => {
  supabase.from("services").select("id,name,category").then(({ data }) => {
    const map = {}; data?.forEach((s) => { map[s.id] = s; }); setServices(map);
  });
}, []);

// After: live subscription + derived map
const { data: servicesArr } = useLiveTable<Service>("services", (q) => q);
const services = useMemo(() => {
  const m: Record<string, Service> = {};
  servicesArr.forEach((s) => { m[s.id] = s; });
  return m;
}, [servicesArr]);
```

The existing `useLiveTable` hook (which already powers all primary data tables) subscribes to `postgres_changes` and re-fetches on any INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE — no polling, no page reloads.

The Card Forge was difficult to read on smaller screens and required unnecessary horizontal scrolling in key control areas. This updates the forge layout to be more mobile-native while preserving the existing vending-machine / arcade presentation.

- **Responsive typography**
  - Increased baseline text sizing for forge controls, labels, hints, and action buttons.
  - Tightened small-screen title/subtitle scaling so headings stay legible without dominating the viewport.

- **Forge control layout**
  - Made prompt pill groups reflow into stable 2-column and 1-column layouts on narrow screens instead of spilling horizontally.
  - Increased pill/button height and padding to improve tap targets and readability.

- **Mobile action flow**
  - Reworked the quick-action row (`Start Here`, `Random Skater`) into a responsive grid that stacks cleanly on smaller devices.
  - Expanded the welcome modal CTA and spacing for easier mobile interaction.

- **Board loadout UX**
  - Switched board-part selection from sideways-only mobile browsing to a fixed responsive grid on phones, while keeping the conveyor/belt visual treatment.
  - Kept the industrial/vending-machine styling by retaining the belt textures, mechanical framing, and neon treatment.

- **Header/nav fit**
  - Adjusted mobile nav spacing and width constraints so the header no longer pushes past the viewport.

```css
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .forge-form .pill-group {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(120px, 1fr));
  }

  .conveyor__track {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
}
```
